/**
 * @mainpage USV Digital Twin - Official Documentation
 *
 * @section intro_sec 1. Digital Twin General Flow
 * The **USV Digital Twin** acts as the computational brain for the Unmanned Surface Vehicle. 
 * The overall system flow starts with the ingestion of official S-57 nautical charts, followed by the generation 
 * of a spatial Navigation Mesh (NavMesh) using Constrained Delaunay Triangulation (CDT). 
 * 
 * At runtime, the system maintains a thread-safe `WorldStateSnapshot`. This snapshot unifies the static map 
 * (via R-Tree spatial indexing), the USV real-time odometry, and the predictive kinematics of dynamic targets 
 * to calculate spatial risk fields and predict collisions.
 *
 * @section arch_sec 2. System Architecture (Separation of Concerns)
 * The project is divided into four main packages to isolate the mathematical engine from the communication middleware:
 * 
 * - **`dt_core`**: The pure C++ central engine (ROS-independent). Handles geometric processing (GDAL/Boost), 
 *   Spatial Indexes, memory-safe Snapshot generation, and collision prediction algorithms.
 * - **`dt_msgs`**: Custom message definitions (IDL) for data traffic on the ROS 2 bus.
 * - **`dt_ros`**: The Adapter Node. Acts as a bridge, subscribing to the USV sensors and injecting translated 
 *   raw data into the `dt_core` asynchronously.
 * - **`dt_viz`**: Diagnostic Graphical User Interface (GUI) developed in Qt5.
 *
 * @section qt_gui_sec 3. Qt GUI & Threading Integration
 * To ensure the Qt GUI rendering does not cause *thread-blocking* issues with the ROS 2 spin loop, the architecture 
 * strictly uses the Immutable Snapshot pattern.
 * 
 * The frontend GUI communicates by requesting `DigitalTwinCore::get_latest_state()`. This returns a frozen pointer 
 * of the environment. The Qt application consumes this data via asynchronous Timers and Signals/Slots, querying the 
 * Spatial Engine (O(LogN)) to draw heatmaps, targets, and alerts without locking the backend data ingestion.
 *
 * @section ros_api_sec 4. ROS 2 API (Topics & Interfaces)
 * The `dt_ros` adapter interfaces with the rest of the USV stack through the following topics:
 *
 * @subsection sub_sec Subscribers (Inputs to the Twin)
 * - **`/sensors/gps/fix`** (`sensor_msgs/NavSatFix`): USV global position (Lat/Lon).
 * - **`/sensors/imu/data`** (`sensor_msgs/Imu`): USV orientation (Euler/Quaternions).
 * - **`/sensors/ais/report`** (`dt_msgs/AisReport`): List of tracked dynamic targets in range.
 * - **`/planned_route`** (`nav_msgs/Path`): The current route (waypoints) planned by the navigation stack.
 *
 * @subsection pub_sec Publishers (Outputs from the Twin)
 * - **`/collision_alert`** (`dt_msgs/CollisionAlert`): Consolidated operational alerts containing Time to Closest Point of Approach (TCPA), distance metrics, and computed risk indexes for each target.
 */